{"schema_version":2,"catalogue_version":1,"id":"bco:24-8","provision":"BCO 24-8","book":"bco","book_name":"Book of Church Order","abbreviation":"BCO","reference":"24-8","title":"Section 24-8","supplementary":false,"canonical_url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/provisions/bco/24-8/","reader_url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-constitution-reader/#bco/24-8","current_text":{"html":"<p>When a ruling elder or deacon who has been released from his official relation is again elected to his office in the same or another church, he shall be installed after the above form with the omission of ordination.</p>","text":"When a ruling elder or deacon who has been released from his official relation is again elected to his office in the same or another church, he shall be installed after the above form with the omission of ordination."},"source":{"name":"PCA Constitution Reader","revision":"edce8a8dcd9ced63bb585bf922e6a97319ef62e1","edition":"Current Reader text","files":{"bco.js":"c88e552545b73fd9690de620b237895b7ea52a94bed8e95690c116bf76be8ae5","wcf.js":"1ebf9e54223f7fe4e728a3e640c833a435af825d74b5ef3d4b04687685538a0d","wlc.js":"f6977e761ea4ccc93b07fcacfd0391890cb05b42f4317d807fa293c078d9b051","wsc.js":"dd775417f7ef21e3283bacad5e6ef193c41d64d03bd5a2e8fb934ccca8cb8e53","rao.js":"49808bbb0e95abdc3b07506c87dde0d62d087851e869b49c0f1f2424986450ec"}},"input_fingerprint":"94a0b54eec213ad53deb08f9fe4e387f46d90e3373f4cd38647b018d7b192c88","parent_id":"bco:24","children":[],"coverage":{"relationships":"indexed_records","recommendations":{"status":"incomplete","note":"Recommendation and study papers are not comprehensively indexed by provision."},"history":"partial"},"relationship_count":2,"relationships":[{"id":"bco:24-8--inquiry:inquiries/ga45_2017__ci08.md","record_id":"inquiry:inquiries/ga45_2017__ci08.md","type":"Constitutional inquiry","title":"Application of BCO 24-1 to the Reelection of Officers","year":2017,"disposition":"advice given","authority_weight":"medium","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/inquiries/ga45_2017__ci08.html","raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/inquiries/ga45_2017__ci08.md","evidence_basis":"structured_provision_tag","relevance_status":"unreviewed","occurrences":[{"id":"bco:24-8--inquiry:inquiries/ga45_2017__ci08.md:occ-a0cab59d0a97","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/inquiries/ga45_2017__ci08.html","repository_path":"inquiries/ga45_2017__ci08.md","locator":{},"excerpt":"BCO 24-1 applies fully to men with no prior official relationship to the church; for men already serving, lower courts determine which provisions apply at re-election.","sources":[],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/inquiries/ga45_2017__ci08.md"}]},{"id":"bco:24-8--case:cases/ga19_1991__1990-08.md","record_id":"case:cases/ga19_1991__1990-08.md","type":"Judicial case","title":"Bowen v. Eastern Carolina Presbytery","year":1991,"disposition":"sustained","authority_weight":"high","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga19_1991__1990-08.html","raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga19_1991__1990-08.md","evidence_basis":"structured_case_metadata","relevance_status":"unreviewed","occurrences":[{"id":"bco:24-8--case:cases/ga19_1991__1990-08.md:occ-847ead965693","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga19_1991__1990-08.html","repository_path":"cases/ga19_1991__1990-08.md","locator":{},"excerpt":"","sources":["cases.jsonl:bco_cited_as","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_current","judicial_cases.jsonl:bco_provisions"],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga19_1991__1990-08.md"}],"metadata":{"topics":["infant baptism","limited atonement","fundamentals of the system of doctrine","officer ordination","annulment of ordination","rescinding prior actions","subscription to confessional standards","ruling elder qualification","deacon qualification","covenant theology","TULIP","five points of Calvinism","original jurisdiction","suspension from office without due process","Robert's Rules rescind motion"],"standard_of_review":"not_stated","case_numbers":["1990-8"],"body":"SJC","synopsis":"Bowen challenged Presbytery’s attempt, two years after installation, to rescind its earlier ruling and annul local officers’ elections and ordinations without trial. The SJC sustained the complaint: ordination is perpetual, deposition requires judicial process, and rescission was out of order after implementation; Presbytery likewise could not suspend a local elder without due process. But it affirmed that infant baptism and limited atonement are fundamentals admitting no officer exception. The officers remained in office but doctrinally out of accord; voluntary demission or proper process was advised."}}],"history":[{"kind":"renumbering","year":2005,"ga":33,"note":"Indexed crosswalk: BCO 24-7 → BCO 24-8.","url":"markdown/ga33_2005.md","status":"verified_vs_corpus","id":"ac374ec6d30797e82334"},{"kind":"renumbering","year":2005,"ga":33,"note":"Indexed crosswalk: BCO 24-8 → BCO 24-9.","url":"markdown/ga33_2005.md","status":"verified_vs_corpus","id":"518c4efcf24031d3b4ef"}]}
